            "role": "assistant",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "output_text",
                "text": "Today is **Monday, August 3, 2026**. Here are the most recent, credible “today/latest” items that touch **Azure AI** (including Microsoft Foundry / Azure OpenAI on Azure):\n\n## 1) Official “what shipped” signal (Azure Updates)\nMicrosoft’s **official Azure Updates** hub is the canonical place to see newly posted GA/preview items across Azure (including the **AI + machine learning** category). ([azure.microsoft.com](https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/updates/))  \nA third‑party aggregator that mirrors official feeds shows at least one **Aug 03, 2026** GA posting (not Azure AI-specific, but it confirms today’s update stream is active). ([azurecharts.com](https://azurecharts.com/updates?monthback=0))\n\n## 2) Latest official Azure AI / Foundry announcements (most recent posts)\nOn the **Microsoft Azure Blog (Announcements)** page, the latest AI-related announcement headlines visible include:\n- **“GPT‑5.6 now available in Microsoft Foundry”** (posted **July 9, 2026**) ([azure.microsoft.com](https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/blog/content-type/announcements/))  \n- **“Claude in Microsoft Foundry is now generally available”** (posted **June 29, 2026**) ([azure.microsoft.com](https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/blog/content-type/announcements/))  \n\nThese aren’t dated “today,” but they are among the newest official Azure AI platform announcements currently surfaced on Microsoft’s announcements feed. ([azure.microsoft.com](https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/blog/content-type/announcements/))\n\n## 3) “Today” enterprise adoption news involving Microsoft Cloud + AI\nA **business/press-wire style** item published **today (Aug 3, 2026)** says **ArcelorMittal** is expanding collaboration with **Microsoft Cloud and AI** as part of its digital/AI transformation. (This is broader than “Azure AI product news,” but it is Azure-adjacent customer adoption news.) ([manilatimes.net](https://www.manilatimes.net/2026/08/03/tmt-newswire/globenewswire/arcelormittal-reshaping-digital-backbone-with-microsoft-cloud-and-ai/2396730))\n\n## 4) Recent platform direction from Build 2026 (Azure AI ecosystem context)\nMicrosoft’s **Build 2026** hub summarizes a lot of “agentic AI” platform messaging and Azure infrastructure/platform updates that support AI workloads (Foundry, agent tooling, etc.). ([news.microsoft.com](https://news.microsoft.com/build-2026/))\n\n---\n\n### If you tell me what you mean by “Azure AI”\nDo you mean **Azure AI Foundry / Microsoft Foundry**, **Azure OpenAI Service**, or a specific service like **Azure AI Search / Document Intelligence / Content Safety**? If you name the area, I can pull the *most recent* items specifically for that product category from the official update feeds.",
